  "static_checks": [
    {
      "id": "admission_before_raii",
      "result": "accepted_static",
      "finding": "try_new_async performs sibling/inherited-source rejection and ADC2 fault recheck, then admit_dac_peer, before constructing the local ADC owner, cleanup writes or NVIC enable."
    },
    {
      "id": "valid_dac_domain",
      "result": "accepted_static",
      "finding": "DAC RCC reset is read before gate write; finite keyed gate enable is retained; actual gate/reset are read immediately before and after typed CR0 read. Both DMAUDRIE1/2 must be false. No DAC register is written."
    },
    {
      "id": "typed_pac_and_rcc",
      "result": "accepted_static",
      "finding": "Actual DAC CR0 typed RW accessor and bit13/bit29 getters match usage; RCC_INFO reads actual register state and uses existing keyed enable_with_cs_readback. DAC domain is distinct from common ADC gate/reset."
    },
    {
      "id": "safe_dac_zero_preservation",
      "result": "accepted_static",
      "finding": "Actual DAC prepare/start full writes start from Cr0 default zero; set writes only DHR; read reads DOR; Drop modifies only output/EN controls. OPA only retains gates and reads DAC. Private RCC and safe SRAM/fixed-serial DMA paths do not rearm DAC IEs. Supporting source hashes still match the accepted design review."
    },
    {
      "id": "inactive_isr_before_mmio",
      "result": "accepted_static",
      "finding": "The unchanged ISR first checks static irq_active inside its critical section; only then obtains registers and reads local EOS enable/status. It masks EOS, verifies once and wakes after the critical section. No sample, caller pointer or DAC MMIO access occurs."
    },
    {
      "id": "shared_fault_leaf",
      "result": "accepted_static",
      "finding": "contain_shared_fault directly latches fault, masks local EOC/EOS and finitely reads raw enables without fallible wrappers. It retires dispatch and leaves NVIC unchanged when masked, disabling only if mask cannot be observed; no recursive call edge exists."
    },
    {
      "id": "completion_and_output",
      "result": "accepted_static",
      "finding": "The existing finite engine is unchanged: waker registration before arming/start and final sticky-EOS check; bounded post-EOS EOC/START polling; local eight-sample staging; verified local masks/selective W0C clear before whole caller-slice copy with no await."
    },
    {
      "id": "drop_forget_reconstruction",
      "result": "accepted_static",
      "finding": "ADC2 async reacquisition retires stale dispatch in the admission/cleanup critical section. ADC2 blocking try_new rechecks fault before RAII, detects irq_active, temporarily enables async cleanup lifecycle, retires dispatch and completes bounded old-async cleanup before ordinary initialize. Errors keep async cleanup semantics and sticky fault. Ordinary Drop performs cleanup before dispatch retirement."
    },
    {
      "id": "adc1_correspondence",
      "result": "accepted_static",
      "finding": "Baseline-relative diff leaves ISR, finite read engine, cleanup helpers and blocking initialize body unchanged. ADC1 Dedicated bypasses new DAC admission/retirement and executes original async_fault body. Blocking owner construction moved into an equivalent FnOnce closure; only SharedDac takes the extra branch."
    },
    {
      "id": "closed_public_api",
      "result": "accepted_static",
      "finding": "ADC2 policy is crate-private and generated, with the existing checked new_async/try_new_async and binding shape; no public guard, bypass, conversion constructor, caller pointer, reset, gate-disable or NVIC pending-clear path was added."
    },
    {
      "id": "explicit_policy_emission",
      "finding": "Only the existing dual_adc=L012 branch calls assert_l012_adc_shared_irq and emits ADC1,ADC2,ADC1,Dedicated plus ADC2,ADC1,ADC2_DAC,SharedDac. Macro signature agrees with the frozen runtime. Other ADC backends and generated branches are untouched."
    },
    {
      "id": "complete_vector_identity",
      "finding": "The helper requires unique ADC1/ADC2/DAC/SYSCTRL identities and their exact addresses/register kinds/versions/blocks; one GLOBAL link per ADC/DAC; unique name/number entries for IRQ12/30; and resolves every peripheral link by interrupt number before comparing the complete IRQ30 owner/link set to ADC2 plus DAC. The prior ADC1 dedicated-owner assertion remains intact."
    },
    {
      "id": "control_domain_geometry",
      "finding": "Exact typed IR checks bind full14-field DAC CR0 geometry, CR1/DOR layout, ADC IER/ISR/ICR sources/access, separate keyed active-high DAC APBEN2 and active-low APBRST2 bit10, and common ADC APBEN1/APBRST1 bit0 with ADC1-ADC2 groups. DAC uses rcc_control without inventing an analog kernel clock. PAC ICR no-op31/reset15 and runtime typed use remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "offset_type_resolution",
      "finding": "The reported initial u8/u32 offset conflict is resolved with u32 byte offsets and checked u8::try_from(offset/4) for the RCC word-offset helper. All later register-geometry calls receive u32. No compilation was needed or run to identify/resolve this source issue."
    },
    {
      "id": "ordinary_example_composition",
      "finding": "Both bins use ordinary Adc::try_new_async for ADC1 and ADC2 with one ADC1 and one ADC2_DAC binding. join composes independent conversions while live Dac owns PB0/PB1. Single reads use caller deadlines/reuse; scan has eight ADC2 slots, repeated external and owned internal handles, per-slot sample times, select cancellation, immediate reuse and later single reads. No HAL probe, mock, test hook or assertion of a timeout winner is introduced."
    },
    {
      "id": "electrical_routes_memory",
      "finding": "Independently read actual CW32L012C8T6/C8U6 generated JSON and Rust metadata. PA0/PA1 are ADC1 IN0/IN1 at pins10/11; PA8 is ADC2 IN5 at pin29; PB0/PB1 are DAC OUT1/OUT2 at pins18/19. Exact packages carry Flash0..65536 and SRAM0x20000000..0x20002000; generic L012 has no package/memory. Board supply3.0..3.6V, VDDA=VDD, HSI/8, qualified temperature and DAC nominal3.3V/load/settling limits remain explicit."
    },
    {
      "id": "cargo_and_linker",
      "finding": "Actual unchanged manifests forward exactly C8T6/C8U6 to HAL and PAC, require async for the two bins and retain the pinned executor/time/futures dependencies. async reserves HAL time-driver-gtim1. Both unchanged build.rs files require one exact memory map, emit metadata-derived memory.x and link.x. Existing blocking and dac_steps bins/locks remain byte-identical to Stage90."
    },
    {
      "id": "public_contract",
      "finding": "The frozen contract accurately states checked DAC valid-domain IE-zero admission and retained-gate effect, current-safe-API closure, no DAC MMIO writes, local EOS behavior, mask-failure-only shared containment, static waker lifetime, cancellation/forget/reconstruction and output commit. Main, clean and final54 acceptance are accurately pending; no silicon result is claimed."
    },
    {
      "id": "declaration_scope",
      "finding": "Only L012 ADC2 single/scan overrides become bounded partial, with their own limitations/evidence. ADC1 remains distinct; advanced modes and user-deferred RF/low-power scope are not promoted. The renderer change is the authorized limitation prose only; no renderer execution was performed by this reviewer."
    }
  ],
  "resolved_findings": [
    {
      "id": "rcc_offset_types",
      "resolution": "Explicit u32 byte offsets and checked u8 word-offset conversions resolve the build helper type conflict before compilation."
    },
    {
      "id": "constructor_error_wording",
      "resolution": "Initial configuration/sibling validation rejection is distinguished from bounded abandoned-async retirement that may write and fail terminally."
    },
    {
      "id": "E1_flash_overflow",
      "resolution": "The original E1 link failed by maximum1088 bytes against the real64KiB Flash. A separately reviewed single release-profile opt-level s-to-z change in the ADC example manifest preserved runtime/example semantics and memory. Final E1\u2013E10 passed; the original failed attempt remains retained."
    }
  ],
